# Arbor Research Iteration (Cursor, no API key)

When the user brings a research idea, progress update, or asks to iterate/optimize:

1. Prefer the Arbor skill suite under `.cursor/skills/` (or `~/.cursor/skills/`).
   Entry: `arbor-research-agent` → `arbor-agent-orchestrator` → phase skills.
2. Use Arbor MCP tools when available (`arbor` server): `tree_view`, `tree_add_node`,
   `tree_update_node`, `tree_prune`, `tree_set_meta`, `eval_run`, `worktree_create`,
   `worktree_remove`, `git_merge_branch`, `generate_report`, `open_dashboard`,
   `scaffold_benchmark`. Do not invent Arbor API keys — Cursor is the brain.
3. Persist state under `<project>/.arbor/sessions/<run_name>/` with Idea Tree as
   durable memory. Do not rely on chat history alone.
4. Idea discipline: mechanism-level hypotheses (Mechanism / Hypothesis / Observable /
   Conflicts), not parameter tweaks. Read constraints via tree view before IDEATE.
5. Eval discipline: iterate on B_dev; use B_test only for merge/final verification.
   Run experiments in isolated git worktrees; protect eval/data paths.
6. Capture findings (leverage/pitfall) into session experience so later runs can recall.
7. Before training, package installs, or B_test, ask the user unless they already approved.

If MCP is unavailable, fall back to
`arbor-agent-tools/scripts/arbor_state.py` for tree/eval/worktree/merge/report.
